  "answer": "Before broad TutorChat rollout for an Enterprise customer, NovaLearn should:\n\n1. Complete SSO and permission audits for enterprise accounts, since Enterprise TutorChat adoption is currently low (44%) because several accounts are running limited pilots pending these audits [NL-030-S03].\n2. Run the rollout as a pilot in a high-impact department of 100–300 users to validate the deployment and justify the onboarding investment [NL-023-S03].\n3. Finish mapping nested permissions from source repositories (e.g., SharePoint, shared drives) to NovaLearn workspaces, as permission mapping complexity is a known onboarding delay driver [NL-011-S01]; TutorChat enforces role-based access via AD/Okta token mapping and filters out unauthorized document chunks [NL-002-S03].\n4. Ensure SSO is configured via supported providers (Okta, Microsoft Azure AD, Ping Identity, OneLogin) using SAML 2.0 or OIDC, since SSO is GA for Enterprise [NL-002-S11].\n5. Set accurate expectations for collaboration integrations: Microsoft Teams is not generally available and is only in design/planning for Q4 2026, while only the Slack connector is available as a limited pilot [NL-014-S07].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
